WEBVTT

00:06:29.942 --> 00:06:32.126
There are many possible reasons for this.

00:06:32.150 --> 00:06:34.216
One is the Protestant work ethic.

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:37.226
Many Americans deprioritize
relationships at work.

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:39.636
We're focused on being
productive and professional,

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:42.170
leaving connections and emotions
for outside of work.

00:06:42.194 --> 00:06:45.375
VM: And that can make for
a fairly isolating experience.

00:06:45.399 --> 00:06:47.618
AG: We're also more mobile
than we used to be.

00:06:47.642 --> 00:06:50.646
As we move to new jobs,
new workplaces and new cities,

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:54.186
we aren't investing in work relationships
like we did in the past.

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:56.336
A third factor might be technology.

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:59.414
VM: I don't think technology
in and of itself is a bad thing,

00:06:59.438 --> 00:07:02.000
but I think the way
many of us are using technology